  "question": "Which product is the best candidate for an offer next month, and what would it earn?",
  "answer": "**I can't name a product to run an offer on yet, and I can't give a trustworthy earnings figure.**\n\nI looked at the three most overstocked products, because they have the most capital tied up. In each one, every discount band is marked thin, meaning it was shown fewer than 30 times.\n\n- **Hill's Grain Free Tuna Cat Food 15kg** (30 in stock, 24 excess, \u20ac1,479.60 tied up) is the most promising.\n  - Without a discount it was bought in 7 of 61 showings.\n  - At 20%+ it was bought in 4 of 12 showings. The model puts its purchase chance at about 0.189, against 0.108 with no discount.\n  - The 10\u201315% band was bought 0 times in 13 showings.\n- **Acana Lamb Dog Food 12kg** (\u20ac1,626.30 tied up) was bought 9 times in 68 showings with no discount. At 20%+ it was bought 0 times in 10 showings, which is thin.\n- **Royal Canin Salmon Dog Food 12kg** (\u20ac1,616.17 tied up) was bought 5 times in 49 showings with no discount. The 10\u201315% band has only 6 showings, which is thin.\n\nThe discount lift is learned across the whole shop, not for these products alone. The shop-wide lift is about 1.44 at 20%+. Each product's own lift is below 1: 0.93 for Hill's Tuna, 0.86 for Acana and 0.83 for Royal Canin.\n\nI didn't price an offer, so I have no profit figure. The thin evidence wouldn't support one.\n\n**Proposed actions**\n1. Don't act on any of these offers yet. Gather more showings first (Product what-if: `/product/?sku=SKU-PT-0277&tab=what-if`).\n2. If you want a small test, run Hill's Tuna at 20%+ only to build evidence (same view).\n3. Review the overstock list for other candidates (Supply: `/supply/`).",
